      "intent": {
        "task": "Normalize the six finite integer/decimal values and identify the six exponents.",
        "source_solution": "Complete source: finite values give 7*10^9,2.586*10^10,3.0792*10^11,2*10^-2,1.3*10^-3,5.7*10^-5. The remaining mixed/fraction values give 1.025*10^-5,1.(6)*10^-8,1.(428571)*10^-6 exactly. Orders: 9,10,11,-2,-3,-5,-5,-8,-6.",
        "unit_reason": "Finite place-value normalization is one coherent method spanning large and small numbers; the fraction-conversion unit covers the genuinely different mixed-number and recurring-decimal method.",
