    {
      "id": "train-catch-up-speed",
      "source_numbers": [
        "182"
      ],
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "火车延误了 $15$ 分钟。为了正点到站，它必须在余下的 $120$ 公里把速度提高到时刻表规定速度的 $1.2$ 倍。火车实际在这 $120$ 公里的运行速度是多少？",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "text": "$80$ 公里/小时。",
            "figure_ids": []
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "text": "$480$ 公里/小时。",
            "figure_ids": []
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "text": "$96$ 公里/小时。",
            "figure_ids": []
          }
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Infer the actual increased running speed by equating the saved travel time to the 15-minute delay.",
        "source_solution": "Scheduled v>0 satisfies 120/v-120/(1.2v)=15/60=1/4. The difference is 20/v, so scheduled v=80 km/h and actual 1.2v=96 km/h. Scheduled remaining duration 1.5 h minus actual 1.25 h saves exactly 0.25 h.",
        "unit_reason": "The complete catch-up word problem has one requested actual speed; intermediate scheduled speed is not an independent response unit.",
        "concept_blocks": [],
        "limitations": [
          "Selection does not demonstrate independently constructing the time-saving equation."
        ],
        "figure_observations": []
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": [
          "c"
        ],
        "rationales": [
          {
            "option_id": "a",
            "truth": "incorrect",
            "derivation": "Solve 20/v=1/4 correctly to get v=80, then return v without applying the required actual-speed factor 1.2.",
            "misconception": "Reports the scheduled speed instead of the actual increased speed."
          },
          {
            "option_id": "b",
            "truth": "incorrect",
            "derivation": "Treat the 15-minute delay as the entire time available for travelling 120 km: 120/(15/60)=120/(1/4)=480 km/h.",
            "misconception": "Confuses the time to be saved with the total remaining running time."
          },
          {
            "option_id": "c",
            "truth": "correct",
            "derivation": "Let actual speed be u and scheduled speed u/1.2. Then 120/(u/1.2)-120/u=24/u=1/4, so u=96 km/h. This agrees with 1.2 times the scheduled 80 km/h.",
            "misconception": null
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "nested-power-simplifications",
      "source_numbers": [
        "184"
      ],
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "在原式有定义的实数范围内，依次化简\n\n$\\left(\\frac{8a^{-2}}{b^{-3}}\\right)^3\\left(\\frac{b^{-2}}{16a^{-3}}\\right)^2$，\n\n$\\left(-\\frac{9x^4}{2y^3}\\right)^{-3}\\left(\\frac{4y^4}{27x^6}\\right)^{-2}$。\n\n原式要求 $a,b,x,y$ 均不为零。哪组完整结果正确？",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "text": "$2b^{13}$；$-\\frac y2$。",
            "figure_ids": []
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "text": "$2b^5$；$-\\frac y2$。",
            "figure_ids": []
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "text": "$2b^5$；$\\frac y2$。",
            "figure_ids": []
          }
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Simplify both full nested-power expressions, retaining their original nonzero restrictions despite cancellation.",
        "source_solution": "For a,b!=0 the factors are 512*a^-6*b^9 and a^6*b^-4/256, giving 2*b^5. For x,y!=0 the factors are -8*y^9/(729*x^12) and 729*x^12/(16*y^8), giving -y/2. Cancellation does not make the original expressions defined at zero.",
        "unit_reason": "One paired simplification checks the whole nested quotient structure, cancellation and odd negative-power sign; neither expression is reduced to a minor exponent blank.",
        "concept_blocks": [],
        "limitations": [
          "Recognition does not demonstrate producing the full symbolic transformations.",
          "The visible nonzero conditions state the original domain and are not removed by cancellation."
        ],
        "figure_observations": []
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": [
          "b"
        ],
        "rationales": [
          {
            "option_id": "a",
            "truth": "incorrect",
            "derivation": "Compute the first factor 512*a^-6*b^9 correctly, but use (b^-2)^2=b^4 rather than b^-4 in the second factor. With the a factors cancelled and coefficient 512/256=2, get b^(9+4)=b^13. Compute the second complete expression correctly as -y/2.",
            "misconception": "Drops the negative sign of a base exponent when taking an even positive power."
          },
          {
            "option_id": "b",
            "truth": "correct",
            "derivation": "First product: (512*a^-6*b^9)*(a^6*b^-4/256)=2*b^5. Second: (-8*y^9/(729*x^12))*(729*x^12/(16*y^8))=-y/2. All cancellations are valid only under the stated original nonzero conditions.",
            "misconception": null
          },
          {
            "option_id": "c",
            "truth": "incorrect",
            "derivation": "Simplify the first expression correctly. In the second replace (-9*x^4/(2*y^3))^-3 by +8*y^9/(729*x^12), discarding the negative sign, then multiply by 729*x^12/(16*y^8) to get +y/2.",
            "misconception": "Treats an odd negative exponent of a negative base as producing a positive factor."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
